    "waves_held": "Also {{count}} single-cycle waves ({{name}}): raw tones the synthesiser's wavetable instruments are built from.",
    "pack_about": {
      "band": "A walking upright bass, alto and baritone saxophones, a tuba, an electric bass, a honky-tonk piano and a clean jazz guitar: the band behind swing, jazz and lo-fi.",
      "kits": "Two real drum kits: a jazz kit played with sticks, and a brushed kit with snare stirs, brushed hi-hat and ride, and a cajon.",
      "folk": "A bagpipe, a finer steel pan, the Hang, folk harp, strumstick, the Vietnamese dan tranh, psaltery, kalimbas and mbiras from Kenya, Tanzania, Zimbabwe and Mozambique, balafon, ocarinas, harmonicas and a didgeridoo.",
      "synth_waves": "All 4,358 of the free AKWF single-cycle waves, for building synthesiser sounds. The core set already has 207 of them.",
      "electric_pianos": "Three classic electric pianos (a Wurlitzer, a Yamaha CP80 and a Hohner Pianet) for lo-fi, synthwave and house.",
      "choir": "A real choir of soprano, alto, tenor and bass voices singing \"ah\", each voice several singers recorded together.",
      "keys": "Every piano in the free libraries, whole: a Steinway B grand with and without the sustain pedal, two Kawai grands, four uprights, five harpsichords, a church pipe organ and a Renaissance organ, and the Yamaha TX81Z's FM keys.",
      "strings": "The whole string orchestra: violin, viola and cello sections, a double bass and a solo violin, each held, plucked, spiccato and tremolo, and the concert harp, with every loudness layer and take.",
      "winds_brass": "French horn, trumpet with and without mutes, two trombones, tuba, flute, piccolo, oboe, clarinet, bassoon, tenor saxophone, saxello and four recorders, each held, short and with vibrato.",
      "mallets": "Vibraphone with soft and hard mallets and bowed, glockenspiel, xylophone, marimba, two sets of tubular bells, a tubular glockenspiel, hand chimes, wine glasses, a bell tree and the steel pan, with every take.",
      "guitars": "Two hollowbody electric guitars with every loudness layer and take, played plain, staccato, with hammer-ons and behind the bridge, and the Martin acoustic guitar's notes in full.",
      "percussion": "A whole rusty drum kit played every way (sticks, brushes, mallets, rims and chokes), orchestral and hand drums, timpani, cymbals, gongs and every small percussion instrument in the libraries."
    },
